    {
      "index": 4,
      "type": "figure",
      "narration": "Then dry the scope, with an alcohol flush where the protocol specifies, followed by forced air through every channel. Residual moisture lets waterborne organisms, especially Pseudomonas, multiply between uses. A coiled scope retains fluid. So store it hanging vertically, uncoiled, valves removed, in a controlled drying cabinet.",
      "audioFile": "audio/vo/ms-cssd-15/V804/scene-4.mp3",
      "voDurationInSeconds": 24.624,
      "voDurationInFrames": 739,
      "leadFrames": 26,
      "tailFrames": 44,
      "durationInFrames": 809,
      "startFrame": 1486,
      "captions": [
